harlots.The word {zanoth,} rendered harlots, is here translated by the
Targumist, the best judge in this case, {pundekon,}
"tavern-keepers:"  see on Jos 2:1.

apes.{Kophim,} rather monkeys, the same as the Syriac [qwp',]
Greek [kephos,] [kepos,] or [kebos,] and Roman {Cephus,} which
animal both Pliny and Solinus inform us was brought from
Ethiopia.  The same name appears in the monkeys, called
{KEIIIEN} in the Prænestine Pavement, and in the French {cep}
or {ceb.}
